[Event "01. What the opposition is (1/10)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/4k3/8/4K3/3P4/8/8 b - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. What the opposition is (1/10)"]
[LineDescription "When the black king must move, it gives up ground: use it to walk your king forward."]

{Welcome! This course teaches one idea: the direct opposition. Two kings on one
file with one square between them cannot step forward, so the side that has to
move must give way. You play White in every line, to the end. Every help is on
in this lesson: the idea in words, a question to guide you, and colours on the
board. Pawn on d3. Black moves first; then win. Two kings are contesting the
same narrow road, with one square between them. Who will have to give ground
first? Red arrows: tempting moves that only draw.} 1... Kd6 {[%cal
Re4f5,Re4f4,Rd3d4] Black has to move, so its king steps aside.} 2. Kd4 {Kd4! —
Take the opposition: the kings face across d5. Black must give way. Kf5? — Black
gets the opposition. Only a draw now.} 2... Kc6 {Black steps aside, but its king
still guards d5.} 3. Ke5 {Ke5 — Your king walks forward, next to the pawn's
path.} 3... Kd7 {[%cal Re5f6,Re5f5,Rd3d4] Black's king gets back in front of the
pawn.} 4. Kd5 {Kd5! — Take the opposition again, across d6.} 4... Kc7 {[%cal
Rd3d4] Black steps aside, still near the d-file.} 5. Ke6 {Ke6! — King first:
your king goes ahead before the pawn moves.} 5... Kc6 {[%cal Re6e7,Re6f7,Re6f6]
Black's king comes forward to guard d5, d6 and d7.} 6. d4 {d4! — Now the pawn
steps forward, with your king ahead of it.} 6... Kc7 {[%cal Re6f7,Re6f6] Black
steps back. Your king guards the pawn's path: d5, d6, d7.} 7. d5 {d5! — The pawn
steps up, protected by your king.} 7... Kd8 {[%cal Re6f7,Re6f6,Rd5d6] Black
stands in front of the pawn, on d8.} 8. Kd6 {Kd6! — Take the opposition across
d7; your king also protects the pawn.} 8... Kc8 {Black steps aside, but still
watches d7 and d8.} 9. Ke7 {Ke7 — Your king guards d8, the promotion square.}
9... Kb7 {Black heads for your pawn from the side.} 10. d6 {d6 — Protected by
your king, the pawn steps up. The finish is in sight!} 10... Kc6 {[%cal
Re7d8,Re7e8] Black attacks the pawn, but your king protects it.} 11. d7 {d7! —
The pawn reaches d7, still protected by your king.} 11... Kd5 {Black is too late
to stop the pawn.} 12. d8=Q+ {Queen! With check, and your king protects the new
queen.} *

[Event "01. What the opposition is (2/10)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3k4/8/5P2/3K4/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. What the opposition is (2/10)"]
[LineDescription "Clear the road with your king first; then your pawn can advance with support."]

{[%cal Rf6f7,Rd5c6,Rd5e6] Pawn on f6. White to move and win. Your pawn is near
the finish, but Black guards the road. Can your king take the opposition and
clear the way?} 1. Kd6 {Kd6! — Take the opposition: the kings face across d7.
f7? — Black's king attacks the f-pawn. Only a draw now.} 1... Ke8 {[%cal Rf6f7]
Black cannot step forward, so it steps aside.} 2. Ke6 {Ke6! — Take the
opposition again, and protect your pawn. Black must give way.} 2... Kf8 {[%cal
Re6d7,Re6d6] Black steps in front of the pawn, on f8.} 3. f7 {f7! — The pawn
steps up, protected by your king.} 3... Kg7 {[%cal Rf7f8] Black has only one
move, away from f8.} 4. Ke7 {Ke7! — Your king guards f8, the promotion square.}
4... Kg6 {Black cannot stop the pawn now.} 5. f8=Q {Queen! The pawn reaches f8,
and your king protects the new queen.} *

[Event "01. What the opposition is (3/10)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2k5/8/8/1K1P4/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. What the opposition is (3/10)"]
[LineDescription "A diagonal step can take the opposition too. Let your king win the way before the pawn moves."]

{[%cal Rb5a6,Rb5b6,Rb5c5] Pawn on d5. White to move and win. Black's king guards
the road ahead of your pawn. Take the opposition first; this time the step is
not straight. Which step is it?} 1. Kc6 {Kc6! — Take the opposition with a
diagonal step: the kings face across c7. Ka6? — Black's king blocks the d-pawn.
Only a draw now.} 1... Kb8 {[%cal Rd5d6] Black steps aside, away from the
d-file.} 2. Kd6 {[%also Kd7] Kd6! — Your king steps in front of the pawn and
guards c7. Kd7 wins just as fast.} 2... Kb7 {Black comes closer, but your king
protects the pawn.} 3. Ke7 {Ke7 — Your king guards the pawn's path: d6, d7 and
d8.} 3... Kb6 {[%cal Re7d8,Re7e8] Black stays near your pawn. Is it safe?} 4. d6
{d6! — The pawn steps up, protected by your king.} 4... Kc5 {[%cal Re7d8,Re7e8]
Black attacks the pawn, but your king protects it.} 5. d7 {d7! — The pawn steps
up; your king guards d8.} 5... Kd4 {Black cannot reach d8 in time.} 6. d8=Q+
{Queen! With check, and your king protects the new queen.} *

[Event "01. What the opposition is (4/10)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/7k/8/7K/6P1/8/8 b - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. What the opposition is (4/10)"]
[LineDescription "Keep king and pawn working as a team: one holds ground while the other advances."]

{Pawn on g3. Black moves first; then win. The kings face each other on the
h-file, with h5 between them. Can your king escort the g-pawn past Black's
defence?} 1... Kg6 {[%cal Rg3g4] Black has to move. It steps aside, in front of
your pawn.} 2. Kg4 {Kg4! — Take the opposition, and keep the pawn protected.
Black must give way. g4? — Black gets the opposition. Only a draw now.} 2... Kf6
{Black steps aside, but still guards g5.} 3. Kh5 {Kh5 — g5 is guarded, so your
king goes round, and the pawn waits.} 3... Kg7 {[%cal Rg3g4] Black gets back in
front of the pawn.} 4. Kg5 {Kg5! — Take the opposition again, across g6.} 4...
Kh7 {[%cal Rg3g4] Black steps aside, still guarding g6 and g7.} 5. Kf6 {Kf6! —
Your king goes ahead and guards g5, g6 and g7.} 5... Kh8 {[%cal Rf6e7] Black
retreats to the corner.} 6. g4 {[%also Kg6] g4! — The pawn steps up, far from
Black's king. Kg6 wins just as fast.} 6... Kg8 {[%cal Rf6e7,Rf6e6] Black gets in
front of the pawn again.} 7. Kg6 {Kg6! — Take the opposition again: the kings
face across g7.} 7... Kh8 {Black steps aside, back into the corner.} 8. Kh6
{[%also g5] Kh6 — Take the opposition again: Black can only go to g8. g5 wins
just as fast.} 8... Kg8 {Black's only move, back in front of the pawn.} 9. g5
{g5 — The pawn steps up, protected by your king.} 9... Kf7 {Black guards the
pawn's path: g6, g7 and g8.} 10. Kh7 {[%also g6+] Kh7 — Your king also guards
g6, g7, g8. g6+ wins just as fast.} 10... Ke6 {[%cal Rh7g8,Rh7h8] Black steps
away from the pawn's path.} 11. g6 {g6! — The pawn steps up, right next to your
king.} 11... Ke5 {Black's king is too slow to catch the pawn.} 12. g7 {g7 — The
pawn reaches g7; your king guards g8.} 12... Ke4 {Nothing can stop the pawn
now.} 13. g8=Q {Queen! The pawn reaches g8, and your king protects the new
queen.} *

[Event "01. What the opposition is (5/10)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
