[FEN "k7/8/1P6/K7/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. What the opposition is (5/10)"]
[LineDescription "Even near the corner, a well-placed king clears the way for its pawn."]

{[%cal Rb6b7,Ra5b5] Pawn on b6. White to move and win. Black's king sits in the
corner, next to your pawn's path. Can your king take the opposition and escort
the pawn?} 1. Ka6 {Ka6! — Take the opposition and guard b7. Black must give way.
b7+?? — Black takes the pawn. Only a draw now.} 1... Kb8 {Black steps in front
of the pawn, on b8.} 2. b7 {b7 — The pawn steps up, protected by your king.}
2... Kc7 {[%cal Rb7b8] Black's only move: it has to leave b8.} 3. Ka7 {Ka7! —
Your king guards b8, the promotion square.} 3... Kc6 {Black cannot stop the pawn
now.} 4. b8=Q {Queen! The pawn reaches b8, and your king protects the new
queen.} *

[Event "01. What the opposition is (6/10)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "6k1/8/8/7K/5P2/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. What the opposition is (6/10)"]
[LineDescription "Let your king lead the way: one wrong step hands Black the opposition."]

{[%cal Rh5h6,Rh5g5,Rf4f5] Pawn on f4. White to move and win. Your f-pawn needs
an escort. Can your king take the opposition before Black blocks the road?} 1.
Kg6 {Kg6! — Take the opposition across g7, ahead of your pawn. Kg5? — Black gets
the opposition. Only a draw now.} 1... Kh8 {Black steps aside, away from the
f-file.} 2. Kf6 {[%also Kf7,f5] Kf6 — Your king steps onto the f-file, ahead of
the pawn. Kf7 and f5 win just as fast.} 2... Kh7 {Black comes out of the corner,
still far from the pawn.} 3. f5 {f5 — The pawn steps up, protected by your
king.} 3... Kh6 {Black tries to reach your pawn from the side.} 4. Ke7 {Ke7 —
Your king guards the pawn's path: f6, f7 and f8.} 4... Kg5 {[%cal
Re7e8,Re7f8,Re7f7] Black attacks your pawn. Can you save it?} 5. f6 {f6! — The
pawn steps up, protected by your king.} 5... Kf4 {Black's king is left behind
the pawn.} 6. f7 {f7 — One step from the finish, and your king guards f8.} 6...
Ke4 {Too late: Black cannot stop the pawn.} 7. f8=Q {Queen! The pawn reaches f8,
and your king protects the new queen.} *

