[LineName "01. What the opposition is (7/10)"]
[LineDescription "Hold the important squares with your king, and advance the pawn when the path is safe."]

{[%cal Rg6g5,Rg6f5,Rd5d6] Pawn on d5. White to move and win. Your d-pawn wants
to reach d8, but Black's king can come back to block it. Can your king hold the
road first?} 1. Kf6 {Kf6! — Take the opposition: the kings face across f7. d6? —
Black answers Ke8 and holds the draw.} 1... Ke8 {[%cal Rd5d6] Black steps aside,
toward the d-file.} 2. Ke6 {Ke6! — Take the opposition again, and protect your
pawn.} 2... Kd8 {[%cal Re6f7,Re6f6,Rd5d6] Black steps in front of the pawn, on
d8.} 3. Kd6 {Kd6! — Take the opposition from the square in front of your pawn.}
3... Kc8 {Black steps aside, but still watches d7 and d8.} 4. Ke7 {Ke7 — Your
king guards d8, the promotion square.} 4... Kb7 {Black heads for your pawn from
the side.} 5. d6 {d6 — The pawn steps up, protected by your king on e7.} 5...
Kc6 {[%cal Re7d8,Re7e8] Black attacks the pawn, but your king protects it.} 6.
d7 {d7! — The pawn reaches d7; your king guards d8.} 6... Kd5 {Black is too late
to stop the pawn.} 7. d8=Q+ {Queen! With check, and your king protects the new
queen.} *

