[LineName "02. How to take the opposition (3/15)"]
[LineDescription "The right king move does not always go forward: a sideways step can take the opposition."]

{[%cal Rc3c4] Pawn on c3. White to move and win. Take the opposition. The right
king move does not always go forward. When the kings face each other, who should
be to move?} 1. Kb6 {Kb6! — Take the opposition. c4? — Black's king blocks the
c-pawn. Only a draw now.} 1... Ka8 2. Kc6 {[%also Kc7,c4]} 2... Ka7 3. c4 Ka6 4.
c5 Ka5 5. Kb7 {[%also Kd7]} 5... Kb4 {[%cal Rb7b8,Rb7c8,Rb7c7]} 6. c6 {c6! —
Your king protects the c-pawn.} 6... Kc3 7. c7 Kd4 8. c8=Q {Queen! Your king
protects the new queen, and the win is easy now.} *

[Event "02. How to take the opposition (4/15)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/7k/8/7K/6P1/8/8/8 b - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. How to take the opposition (4/15)"]
[LineDescription "Answer Black's step to the side and keep the opposition."]

{Pawn on g4. Black moves first; then win. You have the opposition: Black must
move and give way. When Black steps aside, take it again. If it were your move,
it would only be a draw. When the kings face each other, who should be to move?}
1... Kg7 {[%cal Rg4g5]} 2. Kg5 {Kg5! — Take the opposition. Black must give way.
g5? — Black gets the opposition. Only a draw now.} 2... Kh7 3. Kf6 Kh6 {[%cal
Rf6e7,Rf6f7,Rf6e6]} 4. g5+ {g5+! — Your king protects the g-pawn.} 4... Kh7
{[%cal Rf6e7,Rf6e6,Rg5g6]} 5. Kf7 {Kf7! — Take the opposition.} 5... Kh8 {[%cal
Rg5g6]} 6. Kg6 Kg8 7. Kh6 Kf7 8. Kh7 {[%also g6+]} 8... Ke6 {[%cal Rh7g8,Rh7h8]}
9. g6 Ke5 10. g7 Ke4 11. g8=Q {Queen! Your king protects the new queen, and the
win is easy now.} *

[Event "02. How to take the opposition (5/15)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/2k5/8/8/2PK4/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. How to take the opposition (5/15)"]
[LineDescription "A diagonal step that takes the opposition makes Black give way."]

{[%cal Rc4c5,Rd4d5,Rd4e5] Pawn on c4. White to move and win. Take the opposition
with the step that leaves Black to move. When the kings face each other, who
should be to move?} 1. Kc5 {Kc5! — Take the opposition. Black must give way. c5?
— Black answers Kd8 and holds the draw.} 1... Kd7 2. Kb6 Kc8 {[%cal
Rb6a7,Rb6a6]} 3. Kc6 {[%also c5] Kc6! — Take the opposition. c5 wins just as
fast.} 3... Kb8 4. Kd7 Kb7 {[%cal Rd7d8]} 5. c5 Ka6 {[%cal Rd7c8,Rd7d8]} 6. c6
{c6! — Your king protects the c-pawn.} 6... Kb5 {[%cal Rd7c8,Rd7d8]} 7. c7 {c7!
— The c-pawn runs: the king cannot catch it.} 7... Kc4 8. c8=Q+ {Queen! Your
king protects the new queen, and the win is easy now.} *

[Event "02. How to take the opposition (6/15)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "4k3/8/8/4K3/8/4P3/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "02. How to take the opposition (6/15)"]
[LineDescription "You found the opposition square without the idea being named."]

{[%cal Re3e4] Pawn on e3. White to move and win. When the kings face each other,
who should be to move?} 1. Ke6 {Ke6! — Take the opposition. e4? — Black gets the
opposition. Only a draw now.} 1... Kf8 2. e4 Kg7 3. e5 Kg6 4. Kd7 Kf5 {[%cal
Rd7d8,Rd7e8,Rd7e7]} 5. e6 {e6! — Your king protects the e-pawn.} 5... Ke4 6. e7
Ke5 7. e8=Q+ {Queen! Your king protects the new queen, and the win is easy now.}
*

