{[%cal Ra5a6,Ra5b6,Rd2d3] Pawn on d2. White to move and win. When the kings face
each other, who should be to move?} 1. Kb5 {Kb5! — Take the opposition. Ka6? —
Black gets the opposition. Only a draw now.} 1... Kb2 {[%cal Rd2d3]} 2. d4 {d4!
— The d-pawn runs: the king cannot catch it.} 2... Kc3 {[%cal
Rb5a6,Rb5b6,Rb5c6]} 3. d5 Kd4 {[%cal Rb5a6,Rb5b6,Rb5a5]} 4. d6 Kd5 {[%cal
Rb5a6,Rb5b6,Rb5a5]} 5. d7 Kd4 6. d8=Q+ {Queen! The black king cannot take it,
and the win is easy now.} *

