[LineName "07. Long lines (6/10)"]
[LineDescription "One wrong step hands Black the opposition: accuracy from the first move."]

{Pawn on f3. White to move and win.} 1. Ka4 {Ka4! — Take the opposition. Black
must give way. Kb4? — Black gets the opposition. Only a draw now.} 1... Kb6 2.
Kb4 {Kb4! — Take the opposition again.} 2... Kc6 3. Kc4 {Kc4! — Take the
opposition again.} 3... Kd6 4. Kd4 Ke6 5. Ke4 Kf6 6. Kf4 Ke6 7. Kg5 Kf7 8. Kf5
{Kf5! — Take the opposition.} 8... Kg7 9. Ke6 Kg6 10. f4 Kg7 11. f5 Kf8 12. Kf6
Kg8 13. Ke7 Kg7 14. f6+ {f6+! — Your king protects the f-pawn.} 14... Kg6 15. f7
{f7! — Your king keeps the f-pawn protected.} 15... Kf5 16. f8=Q+ {Queen! Your
king protects the new queen, and the win is easy now.} *

